  "explanations": {
    "gnostral": "Since patch 0004 the gnostral lane uses Numerics::CandleCompat: exact integer lanes in Candle's AVX2 order (any ISA) combined with Candle's per-lane fma and hsum_float_8 (or vec_dot_unopt without AVX2+FMA). Unit tests transcribe Candle's intrinsics and assert bit equality per dot, per grouped FFN and per engine forward; this run shows 32/32 token identity end to end. The two late divergences of the earlier Native run are therefore attributed to float combination order.",
    "baseline_upstream_cpu_path": "Established by code inspection, not by a numerical test: on x86 CPU the upstream MoE path (mistralrs-quant gguf/cpu.rs qtensor_indexed_moe_forward) falls back to dequantising the whole Q2_K/Q3_K expert stack to F32 on every call and keeps F32 activations, while the residency path quantises activations to Q8_K as ggml does. Different numerics; no defect is claimed for either path."
  },
